# NPM registry mirror (frontend & social)

## Primary mirror

`https://mirror.abrha.net/repository/npm/`

Used for the **pnpm monorepo** (frontend, social, shared `packages/*`). **Backend** (`apps/backend`) uses **npm** in its own directory and is configured separately (Liara mirror in Docker).

## Fallback order

When the primary mirror fails, try in order:

1. `https://mirror.abrha.net/repository/npm/`
2. `https://package-mirror.liara.ir/repository/npm/`
3. `https://mirror-npm.runflare.com/`
4. `https://registry.npmjs.org/`

## Local development

### Daily install (primary mirror only)

Root [`.npmrc`](../../.npmrc) sets the Abrha registry for `pnpm install` at the monorepo root.

```bash
pnpm install
pnpm install --filter @repo/frontend...
pnpm install --filter @repo/social...
```

### Install with fallback (restricted networks)

```bash
pnpm run install:frontend
pnpm run install:social
pnpm run install:workspace
```

These run [`.cursor/scripts/pnpm-install-with-fallback.sh`](../../.cursor/scripts/pnpm-install-with-fallback.sh), which wraps [`.cursor/docker/fallback-registry.sh`](../../.cursor/docker/fallback-registry.sh) (same chain as Docker builds).

On Windows, use **Git Bash** or WSL for the fallback script.

## Docker & CI

| App | Dockerfile | CI |
|-----|------------|-----|
| Frontend | [`apps/frontend/main.Dockerfile`](../../apps/frontend/main.Dockerfile), [`dev.Dockerfile`](../../apps/frontend/dev.Dockerfile) | GitLab `frontend:build`, GitHub `frontend-cicd.yml` |
| Social | [`apps/social/main.Dockerfile`](../../apps/social/main.Dockerfile) | GitLab `social:build` |

See also [docker-frontend-build.mdc](docker-frontend-build.mdc) and [docker-social-build.mdc](docker-social-build.mdc).

Override via build args / CI variables: `NPM_REGISTRY_URL`, `NPM_REGISTRY_SECOND_FALLBACK_URL`, `NPM_REGISTRY_THIRD_FALLBACK_URL`, `NPM_REGISTRY_FALLBACK_URL`.
